.B ARCHIVE
Required argument
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B MEMBERS
Optional argument(s)
.UNINDENT
.SS ibpwcrk
.sp
Recover the password of an encrypted InstallBuilder installer by brute force.
.sp
Prints the password and exits 0 when found, or exits 1 when the keyspace is exhausted. Without
\fB\-\-wordlist\fP the keyspace is every string over \fB\-\-charset\fP from \fB\-\-min\-length\fP to
\fB\-\-max\-length\fP\&. With \fB\-\-wordlist\fP the entries are tried directly, optionally expanded by
\fB\-\-rule\fP transforms and/or joined by \fB\-\-combinator\fP\&.
.sp
Usage
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
dade bitrock ibpwcrk [OPTIONS] ARCHIVE
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-wordlist <wordlist>
Try each line of this wordlist instead of a generated keyspace.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-charset <charset>
Character set for brute force: a preset (digits, lower, upper, alpha, alnum, printable) or literal characters.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-min\-length <min_length>
Shortest candidate length.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Default
\fB1\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-max\-length <max_length>
Longest candidate length.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Default
\fB16\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-rule <rules>
Word\-mangling rule to apply to each wordlist entry. Repeatable. Requires \-\-wordlist.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Options
none | capitalize | upper | lower | leet | append_digits | append_years
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-combinator <combinator>
Join this many words from \-\-wordlist into each candidate (dictionary combinator). Requires \-\-wordlist.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-separator <separator>
Separator inserted between joined words when using \-\-combinator.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-limit <limit>
Stop after trying this many candidates, even if the keyspace is larger.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-backend <backend>
Which backend to use: auto prefers CUDA, then OpenCL, then the CPU.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Default
\fB\(aqauto\(aq\fP
.TP
.B Options
auto | cpu | cuda | opencl
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-device <device>
Ordinal of the GPU device to use, as numbered by \-\-list\-devices. Ignored by the CPU backend.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Default
\fB0\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-list\-devices
List the CUDA and OpenCL devices with their ordinals and exit.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs <jobs>
CPU worker processes (default: all cores). Ignored by the GPU backends.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
Enable debug logging of the search progress.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress progress and status output; print only the password. Cannot be combined with \-\-debug.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Arguments
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B ARCHIVE
Required argument
.UNINDENT
