.SS decode\-textures
.sp
Decode every texture embedded in the lighting file LIGHTING into OUTDIR.
.sp
LIGHTING is a scene\(aqs \fB*_L.PSX\fP companion. Each texture is written as
\fB<CHECKSUM><suffix>\fP and, unless \-\-no\-montage is given, gathered into labelled contact
sheets named \fBpage<N><suffix>\fP for visual identification. Instances naming a palette that
is not present are skipped.
.sp
Usage
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
dade cli decode\-textures [OPTIONS] LIGHTING OUTDIR
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-tile\-size <tile_size>
Geometry each texture is scaled to. Empty keeps the native size.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Default
\fB\(aq96x96\(aq\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-per\-page <per_page>
Number of tiles per contact sheet.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Default
\fB48\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-tile <tile>
