.SS dump
.sp
Write BINARY\(aqs properties as JSON.
.sp
BINARY is a Mach\-O image: an application\(aqs executable, a framework, or a dynamic library, thin
or universal. Every architecture slice is read.
.sp
The report covers the header and its flags, the segments and their sections, the libraries the
image links, its UUID and source version, the minimum OS it declares, the entitlements inside
its code signature, and, for an image bought from the App Store, the LC_ENCRYPTION_INFO command
that says its text is still enciphered. Nothing is decrypted and no code is disassembled.
.sp
Usage
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
dade misc macho dump [OPTIONS] BINARY
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
Enable debug level logging.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Arguments
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B BINARY
Required argument
.UNINDENT
.SS sc\-info
.sp
Read the SC_Info directory of a purchased application bundle.
.sp
Usage
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
dade misc sc\-info [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS dump
.sp
Describe the SC_Info content at PATH.
.sp
PATH may be an \fB\&.ipa\fP, which is read without being unpacked, or the SC_Info directory
itself, the \fB\&.app\fP bundle holding it, the \fBPayload\fP directory holding that, or a directory
holding \fBPayload\fP\&.
.sp
A download holds more than the application: an app extension under PlugIns and a watch app
under Watch each carry an SC_Info of their own, and every one of them is read. Narrow that with
\-\-main\-bundle or \-\-bundle. Naming the SC_Info directory or one bundle directly reads that one.
.sp
Nothing here is decrypted and none of it is a key: the report covers the purchase record, the
embedded Apple FairPlay certificates, and the length and digest of the key material.
.sp
The App Store link is regional where a storefront can be read from an iTunesMetadata.plist
beside the bundle, and falls back to the region\-less form otherwise. Pass \-\-region to give one.
.sp
Usage
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
dade misc sc\-info dump [OPTIONS] PATH
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-bundle <NAME>
Read only this bundle, named in full or by its last component, such as NotificationService.appex.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print JSON instead of a readable report.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-main\-bundle
Read only the application, leaving its extensions and watch app alone.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-region <CC>
Country code to build the App Store link with, such as jp, when the bundle has no iTunesMetadata.plist beside it to read the storefront from.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
Enable debug level logging.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Arguments
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B PATH
Required argument
